        {
          "page": 1,
          "section": "Introduction",
          "quote": "(Ni49.5Ti35.5Hf15)90Nb10 alloys were obtained by vacuum induction melting and vacuum arc remelting using high purity raw materials. Wires with different diameters were obtained by continuous isothermal hot forging, hot rolling and drawing. All the wires were annealed at 650°C for 20 min followed by 550°C for 3 h before testing. The bulk alloy was taken after hot-rolling and was annealed at 900°C for 1 h before testing.",
